From d9ec7d1dd1406e78eb23461bcf331f2f53ba8e3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lumnus <lumnus.org@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 18:57:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 17/51] B70-IP-W4A8: measured kernel shape (W as the DPAS A
 operand), x16 nibbles, one-kernel tile map

On the B70 any elementwise op on an int8 B-operand tile (the nibble unpack of a
column-major weight block) compiles to a ~50x slower kernel. The weights now
feed the A operand (row-major [BN, 64] bytes, unpacked as 16*nibble with one
shift / one mask, exact in int8, the 1/16 folded into the group scale) and the
activation tile is transposed in registers (Out^T = W . A^T). Defaults from the
QFN sweep: 32 x 256, 8 warps, unfused SiLU (B70_MOE_W4A8_FUSED_ACT=0; the dual
accumulator gemm1 is slower). Tile map is one Triton kernel. CPU tests cover
all three weight-load schemes.
